"""comp-axes -- the ANALYTIC-AXIS DIRECTORY + the estate's first axis time-series (NFRA_GRAPHFEED TO-3).

THE GAP (LD-0298 secs 3-4): the estate's analytic axes live in 8+ scattered readers (heat/pulse/
freshness/debris/depth/learns-status/fedobs/debt) with no single entry point and NO MEMORY -- every
axis is a snapshot that forgets yesterday ("the graph substrate is version-travelable; every
analytic axis on top of it is a snapshot that forgets yesterday"). comp-axes is the THIN fix:

  1. DIRECTORY  -- one screen: every axis with its LIVE VINTAGE + top-3 entries + the canonical
                   drill command. READ-ONLY AGGREGATION: this tool computes NOTHING new -- it runs
                   the existing readers and extracts what they already print. A reader that fails/
                   times out/is absent renders an HONEST degraded row (TIMEOUT / READER ABSENT /
                   ERROR), never a silent omission (LAW: silence is not success).
  2. SNAPSHOT   -- each directory run appends one dated row per axis to the append-only history
                   (org/modules/graph/axes_history.jsonl + a per-run S3 mirror object under the
                   globgrph warehouse) -- retrofitting delta-tracking onto every axis at once.
  3. DELTA      -- diff two dated rows per axis: "what got hotter / colder / more dangerous /
                   staler since <date>" becomes a diff of two rows, not a rebuild.

Usage:
  comp-axes                     directory (all axes) + append snapshot rows   [the default]
  comp-axes --no-snapshot       directory only (no history write)
  comp-axes --axes heat,pulse   directory scoped to named axes (others skipped loud)
  comp-axes --json              machine-readable directory
  comp-axes delta [--since D]   per-axis diff: latest row vs previous (or vs last row <= D, ISO date)
  comp-axes --self-test         dev-box pure-logic self-test (no reader invocations)

Vintage discipline: every row carries the READER'S OWN vintage line where the reader is
vintage-stamped (fedobs/learns-status/pulse), else 'live-probe' for readers that measure at call
time (heat/freshness/debris/depth). A stale-flagged source is carried STALE -- never re-badged.

Author: 0.8.0_AE_CloudComp~Z   TO: NFRA_GRAPHFEED.W1 TO-3 (LD-0299)   Date: 2026-07-15
Read-only over the estate; the only writes are the append-only history + its S3 mirror.
"""
